IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcin-common`
IMPORT `wcin-dates`

-- Accident Compensation Act 1985 (Vic): "NOTICE OF INDEXED BENEFIT LEVELS AND OTHER AMOUNTS IN ACCORDANCE WITH DIVISION 2D
-- OF PART IV OF THE ACCIDENT COMPENSATION ACT 1985", Victoria Government Gazette No. S 363 of 30 June 2026, pages 1-8
-- (deposited text lines 9-336 of ../../registers/source-bundle/GG2026S363.txt). The 1985 Act still governs older claims; the
-- deposit does not say which claims, so the governing Act is an input in the seat layers.
--
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE. Every row of the notice that pays or limits a benefit to an individual, with both printed figures and
-- the arithmetic a row states of itself. The rows are split by the day the claim was made, as the notice prints them.
--
-- Covered: ss 92A(4)-(9), (11A), 92AA (death); s 92B(3)-(8) before and on or after 5 April 2010 (dependants' weekly
-- pensions); s 92D(1)(b) (provisional payments); ss 93A, 93B, 93C, 93CA(1)(c), 93CD(4)(a), (5), 93CDA(1)(d) (weekly
-- payments, by claim date and serious injury); s 98C(2)(e), (f), (3)(d), (e), (3B), (7), (8) (non-economic loss);
-- s 99(1)(b), (d), (15) (medical and like services); ss 134AB(22), 135A(7), 135C(2) (damages); s 5A(5) and s 100B with
-- Schedule 1A items 1, 10 and 11 (pre-injury average weekly earnings).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the employer and insurer rows (s 99(5), line 295; s 125(1)(a)(iii), line 298; s 125A(3)(c), line 300;
-- s 129B(7), line 303); the indexation arithmetic (figures as printed). The Act is not deposited; the facts it decides
-- (pre-injury average weekly earnings, the entitlement periods, serious injury, who is a dependant, the impairment rating,
-- the formulas) are inputs.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Gazette's PDF, not the published
-- Gazette. Victoria Government Gazette, published by IVE Group Limited with the authority of the Government Printer for the
-- State of Victoria. (c) State of Victoria 2026. "This publication is copyright. No part may be reproduced by any process
