§ `Accident Compensation Act 1985 -- the indexed amounts from 1 July 2026`

§§ `WEEKLY PAYMENTS (AWE) -- ss 93A-93CDA`

-- Lines 172-254 ($1,700 $1,740 before 12 November 1997; $2,150 $2,200 from 12 November 1997 to before 5 April 2010;
-- $2,930 $3,000 on or after 5 April 2010):
--   "Weekly payments for First Entitlement Period / Where worker has no current work capacity: 93A(1)(a)(ii), 93A(2)(a)(ii),
--    93A(3)(a)(ii) Maximum weekly payment ... / Where worker has a current work capacity: 93A(1)(b)(ii), 93A(2)(b)(ii),
--    93A(3)(b)(ii) Maximum weekly payment ... – less worker's current weekly earnings
--    Weekly payments for Second Entitlement Period / Where worker has no current work capacity:
--    93B(1)(a)(ii) ... before 12 November 1997 where worker has a serious injury – less 90% of the worker's current weekly
--    earnings; 93B(1)(b)(ii) ... before 12 November 1997 where worker does not have a serious injury; 93B(2)(a)(ii);
--    93B(3)(a)(ii) / Where worker has a current work capacity: 93B(1)(c)(ii) ... before 12 November 1997 where worker does not
--    have a serious injury – less 80% of the worker's current weekly earnings; 93B(2)(b)(ii) – less 80%; 93B(3)(b)(ii) –
--    less 80%
--    Weekly payments after second entitlement period / Where worker has no current work capacity: 93C(2)(a)(ii) ... before
--    12 November 1997 where worker has a serious injury – less 90% ...; 93C(2)(b)(ii) ... does not have a serious injury;
--    93C(2)(c)(ii); 93C(2)(d)(ii) ... Where worker has a current work capacity ... 93CD(5)(a)(ii), (b)(ii), (c)(ii) Maximum
--    weekly payment for claims made ... where an application under section 93CD(1) has been approved – less 80% of worker's
--    current weekly earnings"
-- Rows not printed, so `not covered`: a pre-12 November 1997 claim with a serious injury and a current work capacity in the
-- second entitlement period; a current work capacity after the second entitlement period without an approved s 93CD(1)
-- application.
GIVEN `the period` IS AN `Entitlement period`
      `the band` IS A `1985 Act claim band`
      `the worker has a current work capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the worker has a serious injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application under s 93CD(1) has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Ceiling row`
`the 1985 Act maximum weekly payment row for` `the period` `for` `the band` `with capacity` `the worker has a current work capacity` `serious injury` `the worker has a serious injury` `approved` `an application under s 93CD(1) has been approved` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period`
    WHEN `the first entitlement period` THEN
        IF `the worker has a current work capacity`
        THEN `answered` (`row` (`by band` "s 93A(1)(b)(ii)" "s 93A(2)(b)(ii)" "s 93A(3)(b)(ii)") 1)
        ELSE `answered` (`row` (`by band` "s 93A(1)(a)(ii)" "s 93A(2)(a)(ii)" "s 93A(3)(a)(ii)") 0)
    WHEN `the second entitlement period` THEN
        IF `the worker has a current work capacity`
        THEN IF `before 1997` AND `the worker has a serious injury`
             THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no maximum weekly payment for this entitlement period, work capacity and claim`
             ELSE `answered` (`row` (`by band` "s 93B(1)(c)(ii)" "s 93B(2)(b)(ii)" "s 93B(3)(b)(ii)") 0.8)
        ELSE IF `before 1997`
             THEN IF `the worker has a serious injury`
                  THEN `answered` (`row` "s 93B(1)(a)(ii)" 0.9)
                  ELSE `answered` (`row` "s 93B(1)(b)(ii)" 0)
             ELSE `answered` (`row` (`by band` "" "s 93B(2)(a)(ii)" "s 93B(3)(a)(ii)") 0)
    WHEN `after the second entitlement period` THEN
        IF NOT `the worker has a current work capacity`
        THEN IF `before 1997`
             THEN IF `the worker has a serious injury`
                  THEN `answered` (`row` "s 93C(2)(a)(ii)" 0.9)
                  ELSE `answered` (`row` "s 93C(2)(b)(ii)" 0)
             ELSE `answered` (`row` (`by band` "" "s 93C(2)(c)(ii)" "s 93C(2)(d)(ii)") 0)
        ELSE IF `an application under s 93CD(1) has been approved`
             THEN `answered` (`row` (`by band` "s 93CD(5)(a)(ii)" "s 93CD(5)(b)(ii)" "s 93CD(5)(c)(ii)") 0.8)
             ELSE `not covered` `the notice prints no maximum weekly payment for this entitlement period, work capacity and claim`
    WHERE
        `before 1997` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the band`
            WHEN `a claim made before 12 November 1997` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `by band` p1997 p2010 pnow MEANS
            CONSIDER `the band`
            WHEN `a claim made before 12 November 1997`                              THEN p1997
            WHEN `a claim made on or after 12 November 1997 and before 5 April 2010` THEN p2010
            WHEN `a claim made on or after 5 April 2010`                             THEN pnow
        `the maximum for the band` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the band`
            WHEN `a claim made before 12 November 1997`                              THEN `printed as` 1700 `then` 1740
            WHEN `a claim made on or after 12 November 1997 and before 5 April 2010` THEN `printed as` 2150 `then` 2200
            WHEN `a claim made on or after 5 April 2010`                             THEN `printed as` 2930 `then` 3000
        `row` provision fraction MEANS `the ceiling row` provision `prints` `the maximum for the band` `less` fraction

-- Lines 230-254: "93CA(1)(c) Minimum current weekly earnings $251 $257"; "93CD(4)(a) Minimum weekly earnings for approval of
-- an application for a worker who has returned to work $251 $257"; "93CDA(1)(d) Minimum weekly earnings for approval of an
-- application for a worker who has returned to work under section 93CD(4)(a) $251 $257".
GIVEN `the row` IS A `Minimum earnings row`
GIVETH A `Printed pair`
`the 1985 Act minimum earnings for` `the row` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the row`
    WHEN `continuing weekly payments for an incapacity arising from surgery (s 164(1)(c), or s 93CA(1)(c))` THEN `printed as` 251 `then` 257
    WHEN `approval of an application for a worker who has returned to work (s 165(4)(a), or s 93CD(4)(a))` THEN `printed as` 251 `then` 257
    WHEN `approval of an application for a worker who has returned to work under s 165 or s 93CD(4)(a) (s 166(1)(d), or s 93CDA(1)(d))` THEN `printed as` 251 `then` 257

§§ `PRE-INJURY AVERAGE WEEKLY EARNINGS (AWE) -- s 5A(5), s 100B and Schedule 1A`

-- Lines 320-336: "5A(5) and Schedule 1A Item 1 Column 3 paragraph (c) Where no rate applicable $2,930 $3,000"; "5A(5) and
-- Schedule 1A Item 10 Column 3 paragraph (b) Deemed pre-injury average weekly earnings for a full-time student at time of
-- completion of course $2,930 $3,000"; "100B and Schedule 1A Item 11 Column 3 paragraph(b) Deemed pre-injury-average weekly
-- earnings for a full-time student at a primary or secondary school at time of completion of secondary school $1,700
-- $1,740".
GIVEN `the item` IS A `Pre-injury earnings item`
GIVETH A `Printed pair`
`the 1985 Act Schedule 1A amount for` `the item` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `Schedule item 1, column 3, paragraph (c): where no rate is applicable` THEN `printed as` 2930 `then` 3000
    WHEN `Schedule item 10, column 3, paragraph (b): a full-time student at the time of completion of the course` THEN `printed as` 2930 `then` 3000
    WHEN `Schedule item 11, column 3, paragraph (b): a full-time student at a primary or secondary school at the time of completion of secondary school` THEN `printed as` 1700 `then` 1740

§§ `COMPENSATION FOR DEATH OF A WORKER (CPI) -- ss 92A, 92AA`

-- Lines 30-70:
--   "92A(4) For a dependent partner of partners in equal shares $759,510 $783,000
--    92A(5) For an orphan child or orphan children in equal shares $759,510 $783,000
--    92A(6) For a dependent partner or partners where there is one dependent child in the following shares: total amount of
--           $759,510 $783,000 / 92A(6)(a) For the dependent child $75,940 $78,290 / 92A(6)(b) For a dependent partner or
--           partners in equal shares Balance Balance
--    92A(7) For a dependent partner or partners where there is more than one dependent child but not more than four
--           dependent children payable in the following shares: total amount of $759,510 $783,000 / 92A(7)(a) To each
--           dependent child $37,990 $39,170 / 92A(7)(b) To dependent partner/partners in equal shares Balance Balance
--    92A(8) For a dependent partner or partners where there are more than four dependent children payable in the following
--           shares: total amount of $759,510 $783,000 / 92A(8)(a) To dependent partner or partners in equal shares $569,650
--           $587,270 / 92A(8)(b) To the dependent children in equal shares Balance Balance
--    92A(8A) Maximum lump sum for dependent children if no dependent partner $759,510 $783,000"
-- The 1985 Act notice splits at four children where the 2013 Act notice splits at five (NOTES.md finding 6).
`the 1985 Act s 92A(4) total`       MEANS `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000
`the 1985 Act s 92A(5) total`       MEANS `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000
`the 1985 Act s 92A(6) total`       MEANS `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000
`the 1985 Act s 92A(6)(a) child`    MEANS `printed as` 75940  `then` 78290
`the 1985 Act s 92A(7) total`       MEANS `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000
`the 1985 Act s 92A(7)(a) child`    MEANS `printed as` 37990  `then` 39170
`the 1985 Act s 92A(8) total`       MEANS `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000
`the 1985 Act s 92A(8)(a) partners` MEANS `printed as` 569650 `then` 587270
`the 1985 Act s 92A(8A) maximum`    MEANS `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000

GIVEN `the dependant` IS A `Dependant kind`
      `the number of dependent partners` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of dependent children` IS A NUMBER
      `the dependent children are orphans` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the column` IS A `Notice column`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the 1985 Act share of the death lump sum of` `the dependant` `with partners` `the number of dependent partners` `children` `the number of dependent children` `orphans` `the dependent children are orphans` `in` `the column` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `is a count of people` `the number of dependent partners`)
        OR (NOT `is a count of people` `the number of dependent children`)
        OR (`the dependant is a partner` AND `the number of dependent partners` EQUALS 0)
        OR ((NOT `the dependant is a partner`) AND `the number of dependent children` EQUALS 0)
    THEN `not covered` `the facts given are inconsistent`
    ELSE IF `the number of dependent partners` EQUALS 0
         THEN IF `the dependent children are orphans`
              THEN `answered` (`amount` `the 1985 Act s 92A(5) total` DIVIDED BY `the number of dependent children`)
              ELSE `not covered` `the notice prints no share of the lump sum for this family, only a maximum: the Act, not deposited, divides it`
         ELSE IF `the number of dependent children` EQUALS 0
              THEN `answered` (`amount` `the 1985 Act s 92A(4) total` DIVIDED BY `the number of dependent partners`)
              ELSE IF `the number of dependent children` EQUALS 1
                   THEN IF `the dependant is a partner`
                        THEN `answered` ((`amount` `the 1985 Act s 92A(6) total` MINUS `amount` `the 1985 Act s 92A(6)(a) child`) DIVIDED BY `the number of dependent partners`)
                        ELSE `answered` (`amount` `the 1985 Act s 92A(6)(a) child`)
                   ELSE IF `the number of dependent children` AT MOST 4
                        THEN IF `the dependant is a partner`
                             THEN `answered` ((`amount` `the 1985 Act s 92A(7) total` MINUS (`the number of dependent children` TIMES `amount` `the 1985 Act s 92A(7)(a) child`)) DIVIDED BY `the number of dependent partners`)
                             ELSE `answered` (`amount` `the 1985 Act s 92A(7)(a) child`)
                        ELSE IF `the dependant is a partner`
                             THEN `answered` (`amount` `the 1985 Act s 92A(8)(a) partners` DIVIDED BY `the number of dependent partners`)
                             ELSE `answered` ((`amount` `the 1985 Act s 92A(8) total` MINUS `amount` `the 1985 Act s 92A(8)(a) partners`) DIVIDED BY `the number of dependent children`)
    WHERE
        `amount` p MEANS `the amount in` `the column` `of` p
        `the dependant is a partner` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the dependant`
            WHEN `a dependent partner` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a dependent child`   THEN FALSE

-- Lines 60-70: "92A(8B) Maximum lump sum for any one or more dependent children or dependent partners or partially
-- dependent partners $759,510 $783,000"; "92A(8C) Maximum lump sum for other dependants $20,000 $20,620"; "92A(9) Maximum
-- lump sum for any other dependants if no dependent partner or dependent child or partially dependent partner $759,510
-- $783,000"; "92A(11A) Compensation of close family members for grief and loss $10,000 $10,310"; "92AA Maximum amount for
-- reimbursement of expenses incurred by non-dependent family members $45,300 $46,700".
`the 1985 Act s 92A(8B) maximum`  MEANS `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000
`the 1985 Act s 92A(8C) maximum`  MEANS `printed as` 20000  `then` 20620
`the 1985 Act s 92A(9) maximum`   MEANS `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000
`the 1985 Act s 92A(11A) amount`  MEANS `printed as` 10000  `then` 10310
`the 1985 Act s 92AA maximum`     MEANS `printed as` 45300  `then` 46700

§§ `WEEKLY PENSIONS FOR DEPENDANTS OF WORKER WHO DIES (AWE) -- s 92B`

-- Lines 71-169. Each row prints a line "for claims made before 5 April 2010" and a line "for claims made on or after
-- 5 April 2010". Before 5 April 2010 the maxima are $2,150 $2,200; on or after, $2,930 $3,000. The calculation rows:
--   "92B(3)(b)(ii) Weekly pension calculation for a dependent partner where there are not more than four dependent children
--    who are entitled to a pension and overall cap applies ... $2,150 $3,000 [before] / $2,930 $3,000 [on or after]
--    92B(3)(b)(iii) Weekly pension for a dependent partner where there are more than four dependent children who are
--    entitled to a pension and overall cap applies ... $1,470 $1,500 [both]
--    92B(4)(b)(ii) Weekly pension calculation for two or more dependent partners, where there are not more than four
--    dependent children and overall cap applies ... $2,150 $3,000 / $2,930 $3,000
--    92B(4)(b)(iii) Weekly pension for two or more dependent partners, where there are more than four dependent children and
--    overall cap applies in equal shares ... $1,470 $1,500 [both]
--    92B(7)(b) Weekly pension calculation for each dependent child where there are not more than four dependent children
--    and overall cap applies ... $2,150 $3,000 / $2,930 $3,000
--    92B(8)(b) Weekly pension for dependent children where there are more than four dependent children and overall cap
--    applies in equal shares ... $715 $1,500 / $976 $1,500"
-- Several "from" figures are not the "before" figures indexed (NOTES.md finding 2).
GIVEN `the dependant` IS A `Dependant kind`
      `the number of dependent partners` IS A NUMBER
      `the dependent children are orphans` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` IS A NUMBER
      `the period` IS A `Pension period`
      `the claim was made before 5 April 2010` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Pension row`
`the 1985 Act maximum weekly pension row for` `the dependant` `with partners` `the number of dependent partners` `orphans` `the dependent children are orphans` `children` `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` `during` `the period` `claim before 5 April 2010` `the claim was made before 5 April 2010` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `is a count of people` `the number of dependent partners`)
        OR (NOT `is a count of people` `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension`)
    THEN `not covered` `the facts given are inconsistent`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the dependant`
         WHEN `a dependent partner` THEN
             IF `the number of dependent partners` EQUALS 0
             THEN `not covered` `the facts given are inconsistent`
             ELSE CONSIDER `the period`
                  WHEN `during the first 13 weeks` THEN
                      IF `the number of dependent partners` EQUALS 1
                      THEN `answered` (`the pension row` (`dated` "s 92B(3)(a)(ii)") `reading` "Maximum weekly pension for a dependent partner" `prints` `the maximum` `shared by` 1)
                      ELSE `answered` (`the pension row` (`dated` "s 92B(4)(a)(ii)") `reading` "Maximum weekly pension for two or more dependent partners in equal shares" `prints` `the maximum` `shared by` `the number of dependent partners`)
                  WHEN `after the first 13 weeks and before the end of three years` THEN
                      IF `the number of dependent partners` EQUALS 1
                      THEN `answered` (`the pension row` (`dated` "s 92B(3)(b)(i)") `reading` "Maximum weekly pension for a dependent partner" `prints` `the maximum` `shared by` 1)
                      ELSE `answered` (`the pension row` (`dated` "s 92B(4)(b)(i)") `reading` "Maximum weekly pension for two or more dependent partners in equal shares" `prints` `the maximum` `shared by` `the number of dependent partners`)
                  WHEN `after the end of three years` THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no weekly pension row for this dependant in this period`
         WHEN `a dependent child` THEN
             IF `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` EQUALS 0
             THEN `not covered` `the facts given are inconsistent`
             ELSE IF `the number of dependent partners` EQUALS 0 AND `the dependent children are orphans`
                  THEN CONSIDER `the period`
                       WHEN `during the first 13 weeks` THEN
                           IF `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` EQUALS 1
                           THEN `answered` (`the pension row` (`dated` "s 92B(5)(a)(ii)") `reading` "Maximum weekly pension for one orphan child" `prints` `the maximum` `shared by` 1)
                           ELSE `answered` (`the pension row` (`dated` "s 92B(6)(a)(ii)") `reading` "Maximum weekly pension for two or more orphan children in equal shares" `prints` `the maximum` `shared by` `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension`)
                       OTHERWISE
                           IF `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` EQUALS 1
                           THEN `answered` (`the pension row` (`dated` "s 92B(5)(b)(ii)") `reading` "Maximum weekly pension for one orphan child" `prints` `the maximum` `shared by` 1)
                           ELSE `answered` (`the pension row` (`dated` "s 92B(6)(b)(ii)") `reading` "Maximum weekly pension for two or more orphan children in equal shares" `prints` `the maximum` `shared by` `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension`)
                  ELSE CONSIDER `the period`
                       WHEN `during the first 13 weeks` THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no weekly pension row for this dependant in this period`
                       OTHERWISE `not covered` `the notice prints only an amount for the Act's weekly pension calculation here, not a maximum`
    WHERE
        `the maximum` MEANS
            IF `the claim was made before 5 April 2010`
            THEN `printed as` 2150 `then` 2200
            ELSE `printed as` 2930 `then` 3000
        `dated` provision MEANS
            IF `the claim was made before 5 April 2010`
            THEN CONCAT provision, ", for a claim made before 5 April 2010"
            ELSE CONCAT provision, ", for a claim made on or after 5 April 2010"

GIVEN `the dependant` IS A `Dependant kind`
      `the number of dependent partners` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` IS A NUMBER
      `the period` IS A `Pension period`
      `the claim was made before 5 April 2010` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Pension row`
`the 1985 Act weekly pension calculation row for` `the dependant` `with partners` `the number of dependent partners` `children` `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` `during` `the period` `claim before 5 April 2010` `the claim was made before 5 April 2010` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `is a count of people` `the number of dependent partners`)
        OR (NOT `is a count of people` `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension`)
    THEN `not covered` `the facts given are inconsistent`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the period`
         WHEN `during the first 13 weeks` THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no amount for the Act's weekly pension calculation for this dependant in this period`
         OTHERWISE
             CONSIDER `the dependant`
             WHEN `a dependent partner` THEN
                 IF `the number of dependent partners` EQUALS 0
                 THEN `not covered` `the facts given are inconsistent`
                 ELSE CONSIDER `the period`
                      WHEN `after the end of three years` THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no amount for the Act's weekly pension calculation for this dependant in this period`
                      OTHERWISE
                          IF `the number of dependent partners` EQUALS 1
                          THEN IF `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` AT MOST 4
                               THEN `answered` (`the pension row` (`dated` "s 92B(3)(b)(ii)") `reading` "Weekly pension calculation for a dependent partner where there are not more than four dependent children who are entitled to a pension and overall cap applies" `prints` `the calculation amount` `shared by` 1)
                               ELSE `answered` (`the pension row` (`dated` "s 92B(3)(b)(iii)") `reading` "Weekly pension for a dependent partner where there are more than four dependent children who are entitled to a pension and overall cap applies" `prints` (`printed as` 1470 `then` 1500) `shared by` 1)
                          ELSE IF `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` AT MOST 4
                               THEN `answered` (`the pension row` (`dated` "s 92B(4)(b)(ii)") `reading` "Weekly pension calculation for two or more dependent partners, where there are not more than four dependent children and overall cap applies" `prints` `the calculation amount` `shared by` 1)
                               ELSE `answered` (`the pension row` (`dated` "s 92B(4)(b)(iii)") `reading` "Weekly pension for two or more dependent partners, where there are more than four dependent children and overall cap applies in equal shares" `prints` (`printed as` 1470 `then` 1500) `shared by` `the number of dependent partners`)
             WHEN `a dependent child` THEN
                 IF `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` EQUALS 0
                 THEN `not covered` `the facts given are inconsistent`
                 ELSE IF `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension` AT MOST 4
                      THEN `answered` (`the pension row` (`dated` "s 92B(7)(b)") `reading` "Weekly pension calculation for each dependent child where there are not more than four dependent children and overall cap applies" `prints` `the calculation amount` `shared by` 1)
                      ELSE `answered` (`the pension row` (`dated` "s 92B(8)(b)") `reading` "Weekly pension for dependent children where there are more than four dependent children and overall cap applies in equal shares" `prints` `the s 92B(8)(b) amount` `shared by` `the number of dependent children entitled to a pension`)
    WHERE
        `the calculation amount` MEANS
            IF `the claim was made before 5 April 2010`
            THEN `printed as` 2150 `then` 3000
            ELSE `printed as` 2930 `then` 3000
        `the s 92B(8)(b) amount` MEANS
            IF `the claim was made before 5 April 2010`
            THEN `printed as` 715 `then` 1500
            ELSE `printed as` 976 `then` 1500
        `dated` provision MEANS
            IF `the claim was made before 5 April 2010`
            THEN CONCAT provision, ", for a claim made before 5 April 2010"
            ELSE CONCAT provision, ", for a claim made on or after 5 April 2010"

§§ `PROVISIONAL PAYMENTS (CPI) -- s 92D(1)(b)`

-- Line 171: "92D(1)(b) Maximum amount for medical and other costs $11,320 $11,670".
`the 1985 Act s 92D(1)(b) maximum` MEANS `printed as` 11320 `then` 11670

§§ `COMPENSATION FOR NON-ECONOMIC LOSS (CPI) -- s 98C`

-- Lines 255-284. The 1985 Act notice prints amounts only for ratings above 70% (permanent and psychiatric impairment), and
-- prints the heading "Permanent Impairment – Calculation of Amounts of Non-economic Loss for Further Injury Industrial
-- Deafness" with no row under it (NOTES.md finding 8).
--   "98C(2)(e)(i) Where the worker's impairment benefit rating is more than 70% and not more than 80% $358,420 $369,510 /
--    $40,120 $41,360; 98C(2)(e)(ii) Maximum amount where ... more than 70% and not more than 80% $759,510 $783,000;
--    98C(2)(f) ... more than 80% $759,510 $783,000; 98C(3)(d)(i) Where worker's degree of impairment is more than 70% and
--    not more than 80% $358,420 $369,510 / $40,120 $41,360; 98C(3)(d)(ii) Maximum amount ... $759,510 $783,000; 98C(3)(e)
--    ... more than 80% $759,510 $783,000"
DECLARE `1985 Act impairment band` IS ONE OF
    `s 98C(2)(e): an impairment benefit rating of more than 70% and not more than 80%`
    `s 98C(2)(f): an impairment benefit rating of more than 80%`
    `s 98C(3)(d): a psychiatric impairment of more than 70% and not more than 80%`
    `s 98C(3)(e): a psychiatric impairment of more than 80%`

GIVEN `the kind` IS AN `Impairment kind`, `the rating` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` `1985 Act impairment band`
`the 1985 Act impairment band for` `the kind` `rated at` `the rating` MEANS
    IF `the rating` AT MOST 70
    THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no amount for an impairment rating in this band under the Act named`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the kind`
         WHEN `a permanent impairment` THEN
             IF `the rating` AT MOST 80
             THEN `answered` `s 98C(2)(e): an impairment benefit rating of more than 70% and not more than 80%`
             ELSE `answered` `s 98C(2)(f): an impairment benefit rating of more than 80%`
         WHEN `a psychiatric impairment` THEN
             IF `the rating` AT MOST 80
             THEN `answered` `s 98C(3)(d): a psychiatric impairment of more than 70% and not more than 80%`
             ELSE `answered` `s 98C(3)(e): a psychiatric impairment of more than 80%`

GIVEN `the band` IS A `1985 Act impairment band`, `the column` IS A `Notice column`
GIVETH AN `Impairment figures`
`the 1985 Act impairment figures for` `the band` `in` `the column` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the band`
    WHEN `s 98C(2)(e): an impairment benefit rating of more than 70% and not more than 80%` THEN `figures` "s 98C(2)(e)(i)" (LIST (`printed as` 358420 `then` 369510), (`printed as` 40120 `then` 41360))
    WHEN `s 98C(2)(f): an impairment benefit rating of more than 80%`                       THEN `figures` "s 98C(2)(f)" (LIST (`printed as` 759510 `then` 783000))
    WHEN `s 98C(3)(d): a psychiatric impairment of more than 70% and not more than 80%`     THEN `figures` "s 98C(3)(d)(i)" (LIST (`printed as` 358420 `then` 369510), (`printed as` 40120 `then` 41360))
    WHEN `s 98C(3)(e): a psychiatric impairment of more than 80%`                           THEN `figures` "s 98C(3)(e)" (LIST (`printed as` 759510 `then` 783000))
    WHERE
        `figures` provision pairs MEANS
            `Impairment figures` WITH
                `provision` IS provision
                `amounts`   IS map (GIVEN p YIELD `the amount in` `the column` `of` p) pairs

-- The lump sum after the notice's maximum: above 80% the one printed amount; above 70% and not above 80% the Act's formula
-- amount (an input) or the s 98C(2)(e)(ii) or (3)(d)(ii) maximum, whichever is less.
GIVEN `the band` IS A `1985 Act impairment band`, `the column` IS A `Notice column`, `the formula amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 1985 Act non-economic loss lump sum for` `the band` `in` `the column` `on a formula amount of` `the formula amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the band`
    WHEN `s 98C(2)(f): an impairment benefit rating of more than 80%`  THEN `the amount in` `the column` `of` (`printed as` 759510 `then` 783000)
    WHEN `s 98C(3)(e): a psychiatric impairment of more than 80%`      THEN `the amount in` `the column` `of` (`printed as` 759510 `then` 783000)
    WHEN `s 98C(2)(e): an impairment benefit rating of more than 70% and not more than 80%` THEN min `the formula amount` (`the amount in` `the column` `of` (`printed as` 759510 `then` 783000))
    WHEN `s 98C(3)(d): a psychiatric impairment of more than 70% and not more than 80%`     THEN min `the formula amount` (`the amount in` `the column` `of` (`printed as` 759510 `then` 783000))

-- Lines 277-284: "98C(3B) Non-economic loss in respect of impairment resulting from an injury in section 90D $6,280 $6,470";
-- "98C(7) Maximum amount of compensation for more than one injury suffered on the same occasion $759,510 $783,000"; "98C(8)
-- Maximum amount of compensation for more than one kind of non-economic loss for the same injury $759,510 $783,000".
`the 1985 Act s 98C(3B) amount` MEANS `printed as` 6280 `then` 6470

GIVEN `the limit` IS A `Non-economic loss limit`
GIVETH A `Printed pair`
`the 1985 Act s 98C maximum for` `the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the limit`
    WHEN `more than one injury suffered on the same occasion`          THEN `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000
    WHEN `more than one kind of non-economic loss for the same injury` THEN `printed as` 759510 `then` 783000

§§ `MEDICAL AND LIKE SERVICES (CPI) -- s 99`

-- Lines 287-297: "99(1)(b) Maximum family counselling and therapy and other support services $10,000 $10,310"; "99(1)(d)
-- Maximum payment to family members for reasonable travel and accommodation expenses to attend a burial or cremation of a
-- deceased worker if more than 100 km from family members residence $6,340 $6,540"; "99(15) Contribution to be made by worker
-- towards cost of supported accommodation $45 $46". The 1985 Act notice has no row like the 2013 Act's s 224(1)(d)
-- (family travel to a hospitalised worker).
`the 1985 Act s 99(1)(b) maximum`   MEANS `printed as` 10000 `then` 10310
`the 1985 Act s 99(1)(d) maximum`   MEANS `printed as` 6340  `then` 6540
`the 1985 Act s 99(15) contribution` MEANS `printed as` 45 `then` 46

§§ `ACTIONS FOR DAMAGES -- ss 134AB, 135A, 135C`

-- Lines 304-319: "Pecuniary Loss (CPI) 134AB(22)(a)(i) Threshold $77,490 $79,890 / 134AB(22)(a)(ii) Maximum $1,744,530
-- $1,798,500 / Pain and Suffering (CPI) 134AB(22)(b)(i) Threshold $74,820 $77,130 / 134AB(22)(b)(ii) Maximum $759,510
-- $783,000 / Pecuniary Loss (AWE) 135A(7)(a)(i) Threshold $85,350 $87,360 / 135A(7)(a)(ii) Maximum $1,921,400 $1,966,550 /
-- Pain and Suffering (CPI) 135A(7)(b)(i) Threshold $69,300 $71,440 / 135A(7)(b)(ii) Maximum $703,460 $725,220 / Damages
-- under Part III of the Wrongs Act 1958 (AWE) 135C(2) Death of a person $1,267,530 $1,297,310". Which of s 134AB and
-- s 135A governs an injury is in the Act (not deposited): an input.
DECLARE `1985 Act damages section` IS ONE OF
    `section 134AB`
    `section 135A`

GIVEN `the section` IS A `1985 Act damages section`, `the head` IS A `Head of damages`, `the column` IS A `Notice column`
GIVETH A `Damages figures`
`the 1985 Act damages figures under` `the section` `for` `the head` `in` `the column` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the section`
    WHEN `section 134AB` THEN
        CONSIDER `the head`
        WHEN `pecuniary loss`     THEN `figures` "s 134AB(22)(a)" (`printed as` 77490 `then` 79890) (`printed as` 1744530 `then` 1798500)
        WHEN `pain and suffering` THEN `figures` "s 134AB(22)(b)" (`printed as` 74820 `then` 77130) (`printed as` 759510 `then` 783000)
    WHEN `section 135A` THEN
        CONSIDER `the head`
        WHEN `pecuniary loss`     THEN `figures` "s 135A(7)(a)" (`printed as` 85350 `then` 87360) (`printed as` 1921400 `then` 1966550)
        WHEN `pain and suffering` THEN `figures` "s 135A(7)(b)" (`printed as` 69300 `then` 71440) (`printed as` 703460 `then` 725220)
    WHERE
        `figures` provision threshold maximum MEANS
            `Damages figures` WITH
                `provision`     IS provision
                `the threshold` IS `the amount in` `the column` `of` threshold
                `the maximum`   IS `the amount in` `the column` `of` maximum

`the 1985 Act s 135C(2) amount` MEANS `printed as` 1267530 `then` 1297310
